  "difference_from_s4b": "This is not the S4b simulated cold start. S4b keeps each evaluated user in the training matrices, truncates the query to the earliest N full-train ratings (N of 5 and 10), and scores the original per-user test split. The user-id embedding is the one learned for that user, and item-item similarities include that user's later train ratings. Here the user is absent from every training row. The model sees only the first N chronological ratings, N in {1, 3, 5, 10}, and is scored on the later ratings with relevance at least 4. There is no user-id embedding at score time, and demographic features are not used.",
